1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:11,800
Compare native A2UI with portable MCP Apps over the same Oracle-governed supply-chain service.

2
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:23,800
A2A connects hosts to agents. A2UI declares native UI. MCP Apps return sandboxed web UI. MCP exposes governed tools.

3
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:35,800
The host discovers A2UI v0.8 and its supported component catalog before it renders any response.

4
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:47,800
The user asks for three recommendations above risk 70. The adapter calls the governed service and returns A2UI DataParts.

5
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:59,800
Move to the recommendation, enter notes, and select the exact-transfer action. The host sends a bounded userAction back over A2A.

6
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:11,800
The MCP server exposes one bounded dashboard tool and points the host to a portable HTML application.

7
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:23,800
ChatGPT displays the Toolkit result and loads the sandboxed MCP App. The cursor selects Review this transfer inside the supplied interface.

8
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:35,800
Claude discovers the same bounded tool and renders the same ui:// dashboard through its connector and sandbox bridge.

9
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:47,800
Create an OAuth-backed private connector, reload custom actions, and enable only show-inventory-transfer-dashboard.

10
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:59,800
The service binds approval to the actor and exact recommendation. Oracle locks, revalidates, audits, and commits atomically.

11
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:11,800
Deep Data Security filters rows by the authenticated database identity before the Toolkit, service, host, or model receives them.

12
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:23,800
Use A2UI for native, catalog-controlled components. Use MCP Apps for rich portable web interfaces. Keep Oracle AI Database authoritative.

